---
title: Associated Data and Media
sidebar:
  label: Associated data and media
  order: 7
---

Use `Associated Data` for specimen-linked digital data that is not better stored
as a specimen part or media record. Examples include GenBank accessions,
MorphoSource records, analysis files, or external database links. It is the
storage-icon tab of the `Specimen Parts` card.

Associated data fields include:

- `Data type`: `Link` or `File`.
- `Name`: source or dataset name, such as `GenBank`.
- `Description`: accession number or description of the data.
- `Date`: date associated with the data.
- `URI`: external URL when the data type is `Link`.
- File selector: local file attachment when the data type is `File`.

{% steps %}

1. Choose the `Data type`.
2. For a `Link`, enter the address in `URI`. For a `File`, select the file. On
   desktop, choose `Copy to project` to store a copy with NAHPU, or
   `Link original` to point at the file where it is; a linked original must
   stay at that path.
3. Add a `Name`, `Description`, and `Date`.

{% /steps %}

Check linked files after a transfer, and look into any missing-file warning. Use
Media, below, for images, audio, and video.

## Media

Use `Media` for photos, video, and audio of the specimen. Add them with
`Take photos/videos`, `Record audio`, `Add from gallery`, or `Add from file`.
Each item can carry a caption, tags, and the photographer's name. Media are
stored once in NAHPU's shared media library and linked to the specimen.
